# Copy to .env. Nothing here is required for the pipeline to run: without a LangSmith key
# it still answers and still guards, and only loses its traces.

# Turns tracing on. Off is a complete configuration; the pipeline behaves identically.
LANGSMITH_TRACING=true
LANGSMITH_API_KEY=

# Deliberately NOT set. The project is derived from the target this pipeline watches, which
# is the name the target itself reports under — so both halves of a request land in one
# project. Setting it here overrides that and splits the trace in two. Uncomment only to
# send these traces somewhere else on purpose.
# LANGSMITH_PROJECT=

# Needed only by the evaluation pipeline, for the LLM judge. The target holds its own key
# and answers without this; leaving it unset means the report prints the judge section as
# unavailable rather than scoring it zero.
#
# The judge stays here on `qwen/qwen3.8-27b` rather than moving to OpenAI below. The target
# answers on `openai/gpt-oss-120b`, and grading an OpenAI model with another OpenAI model is
# a weaker separation than a different family from a different company. A system grading its
# own output shares its blind spots.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# The RAGAS evaluator. Optional: without it RAGAS falls back to the Groq model above, which
# works but is rate-limited hard enough to spoil a run.
#
# Why this was added. Groq's free tier caps this organisation at 200,000 tokens PER DAY, and
# a single full evaluation spends most of it. Runs were dying part-way through with scores
# silently missing, and the gaps were not random: the set is scored in order, so the cases
# that dropped out were the longest and hardest ones at the end — `cashless-claim`,
# `casual-leave`, `harassment-report`. An aggregate over what survived therefore flattered
# the system, which is worse than no aggregate at all.
#
# OpenAI removes three limits at once: no daily cap, rate limits high enough to drop the
# one-request-per-30-seconds pacing, and support for n>1 so `answer_relevancy` can run at
# RAGAS' default strictness of 3 without the `bypass_n` workaround. A full pass costs a few
# cents on a mini model.
#
# Embeddings deliberately stay on Bedrock `cohere.embed-english-v3`. Its similarity scale is
# measured and healthy — 0.977 for a close paraphrase, 0.126 for an unrelated question — and
# changing the embedder would move every answer_relevancy score, invalidating the
# comparisons already recorded in docs/measurements/.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# The guardrail uses the usual AWS credential chain, so these are only needed when that
# chain is not already configured.
# AWS_PROFILE=
# AWS_REGION=ap-south-1
